# LifeOps agent rules

Follow the full project standards in **`AGENTS.md`** (repo root) for every change. `CLAUDE.md` also points there.

## Non-negotiables

- **pnpm only** — never npm/yarn
- **Do not run `pnpm run build`** unless the user asks or the task is build/CI failure
- **Read Next.js docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`** before using Next APIs — this app’s Next version may differ from training data
- **Reuse / extend shared components** — one Input, Button, FormField pattern, etc.; extract on the second copy; no one-off duplicates; use toasts, never `alert()`
- **Spanish product UI** — user-visible copy may be Spanish; **routes, files, variables, types, comments, SQL, and API paths are English only** — no Spanish route segments or Spanish identifier names
- **Human Spanish, few anglicisms** — natural Mexican Spanish in UI/toasts/errors; prefer `correo`, `iniciar sesión`, `enlace`, `archivo` over Spanglish; keep product terms (póliza, asesor, cobranza); see AGENTS.md “Spanish product copy”
- **Folder structure** — `src/app`, `src/components/ui`, `src/lib`, `src/types`, `supabase/migrations`, `docs/`; colocate `actions.ts` with routes for new mutations; English route segments only (`/dashboard/contracts`, `/dashboard/projection`, …)
- **Concentrate I/O adapters** — browser Auth → `src/lib/auth/client.ts`; Auth Admin → `src/lib/auth/admin.ts`; Storage → `src/lib/storage/admin.ts`; tables → `db.ts` / `db-admin.ts`. Do not call `supabase.auth.*` / `supabaseAdmin.auth.admin.*` / `supabaseAdmin.storage.*` from pages or routes
- **Product docs** — if business rules or general LifeOps behavior change, update `README.md` in the same change
- **Database migrations** — every DB change is a **new** file in `supabase/migrations/`; never edit an already-created migration; update `docs/database.md` in the same change
- **Verify Supabase project before push** — before `supabase db push` / remote migrations, confirm project ref/name matches the intended env and local `.env` URL; ask if unclear
- **Validate inputs on the server** with Zod schemas that include **regex + length limits** (`src/lib/validation/schemas.ts`); map failures to **per-field UI errors** via `zodFieldErrors` + `FormField` `error`; sanitize outputs (no unsafe HTML from user data)
- **Image uploads** — decode, strip metadata, resize/re-encode server-side before Storage; reject undecodable / oversized / non-allowlisted files (see AGENTS.md “File uploads”)
- **Backend on the server** — prefer Server Actions / route handlers + adapters (`db-admin`, auth/admin, storage/admin); no GraphQL unless asked; safe Spanish errors
- **Service role is server-only** — `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` + `@/lib/supabase/admin`; never in the browser; privileged APIs use Bearer `authFetch` + `requireOfficeContext`
- **Design system + responsive + a11y** — CSS variables via Tailwind shorthand (`text-(--token)`, `bg-(--token)`, `border-(--token)`); labels, focus, icon `aria-label`s; dark UI + golden accent; primary CTAs via `Button` `variant="brand"`
- **Office tenancy / RLS** — promotory = office-wide; consultant = own data; secrets stay server-side
- **No setState in effects** — `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect`. Reset state during render when a key changes (`useResetPage` / `useQueryLoading`); start fetches with `useQueryEffect` and set state only after `await`. See AGENTS.md “React effects”
